WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.902
-Our next guest is
a fantastically funny

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.670
actress and comedian you know
from shows like

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.339
"Living With Yourself"
and "This Way Up."

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.641
She stars in
"Home Sweet Home Alone,"

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.809
which premieres Friday
on Disney+.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.244
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.014
-I swear to you that boy was
not in the house when we left.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.315
-And where do
you think he was, Stu?

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.119
At the -- at the
Four freaking Seasons?

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.486
-He had the fish curry
on the plane.

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:22.922
We probably got a hard 30 before
we're going to see Stu.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.423
-You do realize that,
because of you,

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.225
I'm in Japan and my 10- --

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:29.762
10-year-old son
is at home by himself.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.765
-Yeah, but -- but first-world
problems, you know.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.600
-First-world...
-Stop it!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.601
Listen, listen! Stop it!

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.070
I got that at Brookstone!

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.471
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.640
our friend Aisling Bea,
everybody.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.410
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.125
Aisling, it is great
to see you again.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.160
-Thank you, Seth.
It is also great to see you.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.895
Well, the first bit's
gone real well!

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:07.600
-We are natural.
People know we're friends.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.235
You're a -- This is a good night
for you to be here.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.538
You're also a Taylor Swift fan.
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.173
I'm the headline act
this evening.

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:15.608
Glad to be here.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.276
I was -- Well, I didn't --
'Cause I didn't run into her,

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.812
which I was kind of happy about,
because the last time

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.614
I saw Taylor Swift was when
I accidentally ended up

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.815
in her apartment.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.517
-How did that happen?
-In her sitting room.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:28.988
And -- Which is not like, "Oh,
that's what I told the police."

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:33.026
I -- Of course
we were going to have

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.894
maybe a moment
where I could explain.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:38.831
-Right.
-But, no, she ran away.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.299
-So she saw you tonight
and remembered,

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.468
"This is the strange woman who
showed up in my sitting room."

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.870
-Well, I think her security
might have, yeah.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.237
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:47.273
-But I --
Yeah, basically, I was --

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.540
When I was doing
"Living With Yourself,"

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.942
I was living in New York.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.312
And my friend was here, and
we were going to go ice-skating,

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.346
And I'd had
a long old day at work.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:57.216
And, so, I was dressed up, ready
for ice skating, kind of --

00:01:57.216 --> 00:02:00.586
you know, your snow boots,
giant, you know --

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.756
paraphernalia, a hat, ice pick,
the whole shebang.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.090
Not an ice pick.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.027
And he was like, "Oh, I'm just
at my friend's house,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.396
having a beer if you
want to come and join us."

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.631
You know, he's an actor.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.433
And I was like,
"Yeah, yeah, I'll join you,

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.801
but what time are
we doing ice skating?"

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.502
He's like, "Oh, yeah, we'll
definitely go ice skating.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.070
I'm just having a beer
at my friend's house."

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.472
And I was like, "Okay."

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.474
And he was like, "Um, yeah, just
come to the door, ring the bell,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.042
and, you know,
someone will come down."

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.510
And I was like,
"Okay, sounds a bit 'cool.'"

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.179
You know, a bit retro.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.714
And then this man came down.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.915
He was, like, a really
big man in the lift.

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:30.916
And I was like, "Oh, hi!

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.418
Thank you so much
for having me."

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.786
He was like, "Yeah."

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.222
And I was like,
"Oh, what a warm man."

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.392
And then we went up
in the elevator,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.661
and it opened and I was in
Taylor Swift's sitting room

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:45.731
with Taylor Swift in her
sitting room playing pool.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:48.467
And I was --
She looked so beautiful.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.737
And she looks and looked like
Elsa from "Frozen,"

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.572
just kind of like,
"Hi, welcome."

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:56.742
And I was there dressed like
Olaf just like, "Aaah!

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:59.612
Oh, my God! Aaaah!"

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.881
And then I --
We didn't go ice skating,

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.881
because we were --

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:04.183
-Why would you? Yeah.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.752
-I kept on trying to look at
my friend, being like,

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:10.022
"Why didn't you tell me

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:13.258
that we were going to be
in Taylor Swift's house?

00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:15.828
I would not have
worn this out...

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.029
Yeah, I'd love
a gin and tonic, Taylor.

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:18.498
Thank you so much."

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:22.802
-It's very rude.
-It is very rude.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.938
Because I'm a massive fan,
so to just turn up --

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.041
And then I've just felt
creepy by my existence.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:31.744
-Yeah.
-So I was like...

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.012
"Lovely smell."

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.980
-I am so happy that
you're here, because you --

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.382
And I'm happy to see
you're recovered.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.817
You did catch COVID.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:38.952
-Yes, COVID.
-In the fall.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.952
-Yeah.

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:41.220
-You had to miss
a lot of things,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.455
so we're very happy
to have you here in person.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.589
-Yeah, I did.
I got the --

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:45.258
Oh, thank you very much!

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.193
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.695
That's all you need nowadays.
I survived COVID.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:53.066
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.767
Yes, I did.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:59.672
Double-vaxxed, but I got
the stars variant,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.106
so contracted that one.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:04.210
And, yeah,
but it was my first week off,

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:08.380
and I'd organized my best
friend's bachelorette party.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.149
And then there was her wedding.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.184
And then the next day
was her son's christening,

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.987
and I'm one of the godparents.

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:17.189
And that was
all during my 10 days.

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.391
-So you couldn't do any of it.
-Couldn't do any of it.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:21.127
But I did -- I was like,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:24.997
"Well, how can I sort of be
there in spirit in some way?"

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:28.334
-And you -- I think this is
a very good solution.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.502
-Yeah. It's kind of like
a new COVID thing.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:34.139
Just send a cardboard cutout
of yourself.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:35.274
-I mean, that is just --

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:36.909
And, also, like,
just a fun cardboard cutout.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.143
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:38.143 --> 00:04:40.713
I'm glitzy. I'm fun.
I'm a great wedding guest.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.115
You know, and people
did say afterwards --

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:46.118
they were like,
"You were so much more chill

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.153
than your normal personality
at the wedding.

00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:49.455
We should hang out more,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.457
yeah, because you were just
better to be around."

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.126
-I notice your co-star from the
fantastic show "This Way Up,"

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.228
Tobias Menzies.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.462
-Tobias Menzies.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.898
-Who is, I will say --
Yeah, Tobias, you know,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.433
now an Emmy winner from
"The Crown."

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.467
-Yep.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.001
-You kind of
knew him when, right?

00:05:03.001 --> 00:05:04.303
-I what?
-You knew him when.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.437
You, like -- You got in on
the ground floor.

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:07.306
-I though you said,
"I knew him win."

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.342
And I was like, "Seth,
that's not great English."

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:11.444
"You knew him win!"
-You knew him win.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.478
You call me.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.880
You call me and say,
"Tobias win."

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.350
You knew!
-You knew him win Emmy!

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.787
So natural.

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:24.490
-Aisling, it's Seth.
You knew him win!

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.491
-You knew him win Emmy!

00:05:26.491 --> 00:05:27.693
-I hang up now.

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.661
-No, stop, stop.
-Mm!

00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:34.634
-Knew him win Emmy,
but, also, yeah, he was --

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.302
He's the other godparent.
-Ah!

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.503
-So, we also -- So, in my show,
"This Way Up" --

00:05:38.503 --> 00:05:39.572
All available on Hulu.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.707
Watch it, please.
-Fantastic.

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:43.709
-He plays
a character called Richard,

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:46.245
and he's also Prince Philip
in "The Crown,"

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.913
which is what
he won the Emmy for.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:50.983
But we're also godparents
together of this child,

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.519
and the other godmother
is actually Emerald Fennell,

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.955
who wrote "Promising Young
Woman" and won an Oscar.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.057
-Yeah.
-So I'm, like, the crappy one.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.158
-Yeah.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.126
-And I'm literally
a cardboard cutout.

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:04.464
So I'm not, like,
the quality beef of godparents.

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:07.266
-Years from now, he'll say,
"So, the award winners came."

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.802
-Yeah, the award winners,
and then in spirit

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.036
was the sort of --
You know the damp one?

00:06:11.036 --> 00:06:15.041
We threw her in the lake,
and she floated, yeah.

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:18.677
So, yeah -- So --
But in "This Way Up,"

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:23.048
the second series I've actually
set in March 2020,

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:24.617
which you find out
as it is goes along --

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:27.687
So, technically,
it's now a period drama,

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.188
and it's a bit more like
"The Crown."

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.356
So that's what I've done.
-Oh, very wise.

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:34.026
Very wise move
for the award pandering.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.394
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:38.163
-Did you -- Making this
"Home Alone" remake,

00:06:38.163 --> 00:06:42.301
was "Home Alone" a film that you
were aware of growing up?

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.771
-Yeah! I didn't grow up in,
like, you know, the North Pole.

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.239
Even the North Pole
is a bad reference,

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.842
because that's where
Santa Claus lives.

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:52.744
Yeah, yeah, I was massive --
But I do think, like,

00:06:52.744 --> 00:06:56.048
at the time,
when movies came out in America,

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.583
you were like, "Oh, God,
it's come out in America.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.419
All we need to do is wait for
one to three years,

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:02.488
and we'll see it soon!

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:05.090
Ahhhh!"

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.392
So, stuff used to come out like
a year or two later

00:07:07.392 --> 00:07:09.895
than America, but, like,
we got, like, to --

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:13.699
If I was to tell
my baby self that,

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.968
"You're going to become
an actor and end up in the

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.838
'Home Alone' movie," I think
I'd really have understood that

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.606
as a sign of things
are going well.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.807
-Yeah, things are
going very well.

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:23.909
Now, I will admit that
not a lot of --

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:25.778
We didn't get a lot of Irish
kid stuff over here.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:27.213
It was not a two-way street.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.147
-That is a giant loss
for you guys.

00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:31.049
-Yeah. Well, you sent this,
and I'm not sure

00:07:31.049 --> 00:07:36.422
it was a giant loss, because I
think this is disturbing.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.557
-Let me tell you something.

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:39.358
You're about to
get canceled in Ireland.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.126
-Okay.

00:07:41.126 --> 00:07:44.096
-These were our children's
entertainer presenters.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:46.264
They hosted
a show called "The Den."

00:07:46.264 --> 00:07:50.670
These are two aliens
who came to Ireland from space.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.006
That was the destination
that they were most --

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:56.609
And then, eventually,
they sort of adopted

00:07:56.609 --> 00:08:02.481
a puppet turkey from Dublin,
who then went on --

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:03.516
Do you know what
the Eurovision is?

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.617
-Yeah.

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:07.186
-Yeah, The Eurovision,
what he does --

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:09.521
The Eurovision is, like,
a massive competition

00:08:09.521 --> 00:08:12.991
of, like, musical things
from around Europe,

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:15.794
plus Australia for some reason.

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:18.163
And we sent Dustin the Turkey

00:08:18.163 --> 00:08:23.536
as our representative to sing
on behalf of Ireland.

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.438
Just in case
you're wondering, like,

00:08:26.438 --> 00:08:29.075
"How could you sum up
a culture?"

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:33.713
We sent him to sing
on behalf of Ireland.

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:34.980
-Yeah.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.049
-But he's a massive --
He's a massive deal there.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:38.551
-How did he do?

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:41.219
-Oh, we lost.
We did not win at all.

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:43.622
-So, he probably finished
highest of the Turkeys.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:44.723
-Yeah, I'd say so.

00:08:44.723 --> 00:08:47.492
Well, you say that,
but then...

00:08:47.492 --> 00:08:48.560
-It is always such
a delight to see you.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:49.595
-Thank you so much.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:50.596
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.798
You guys, that's Aisling Bea.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:55.401
"Home Sweet Home Alone"
premieres Friday on Disney+,

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:56.569
and "This Way Up"
is streaming on Hulu.

